{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-135-1","title":"Psalms 135:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 An exhortation to praise God for his mercy; 5 for his power; 8 for his judgments. 15 The vanity of idols. 19 An exhortation to bless God.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3000. B.C. 1004. (Title.)Bp. Patrick supposes this to be the morning hymn which the precentor called upon the Levites to sing at the opening of the gates of the temple, as the foregoing was sung at the shutting in the evening; but it is more probable that it was composed by Solomon, to be sung at the dedication of the temple.</p>\n<p>Praise ye the Lord. 33:1,2; 96:1-4; 106:1; 107:8,15; 111:1; 112:1; 113:1; 117:1,2; 150:6 Praise ye the name. 7:17; 102:21; 113:2,3; 148:13; Ex 34:5-7; Ne 9:5 O ye servants. 113:1; 134:1; 149:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-2","title":"Psalms 135:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>that stand. 1Ch 16:37-42; 23:30; Ne 9:5; Lu 2:37 the courts. 92:13; 96:8; 116:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-3","title":"Psalms 135:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>for the Lord. 106:1; 107:1; 118:1; 119:68; 136:1; 145:7,8; Mt 19:17 for it is. 33:1; 63:5; 92:1,2; 147:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-4","title":"Psalms 135:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the Lord. 33:12; De 7:6,7; 10:15; 1Sa 12:22; Isa 41:8; 43:20,21; Zec 2:10-12 1Pe 2:9 his peculiar. Ex 19:5,6; De 32:9; Mal 3:17; Tit 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-5","title":"Psalms 135:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>I know. 48:1; 86:8-10; 89:6; 95:3; 96:4,5; 97:9; De 10:17; Isa 40:22,25 Jer 10:10,11; Da 3:29; 6:26,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-6","title":"Psalms 135:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Whatsoever. 33:9,11; 115:3; Isa 46:10; Da 4:35; Am 4:13; 9:6; Mt 28:18 in the seas. 136:13-15; Mt 8:26,27; 14:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-7","title":"Psalms 135:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>He causeth. 148:8; Ge 2:5,6; 1Ki 18:1,41-45; Job 5:10; Jer 10:13; 14:22; 51:16 Zec 10:1 he maketh lightnings.Dr. Russel informs us that seldom a night passes at Aleppo without much lightning in the north-west, but not attended with thunder; and when it appears in the west or south-western points, it is a sure sign of the approaching rain, which is often followed with thunder. See the note on Job 38:26.</p>\n<p>Job 28:25,26; 38:24-28 he bringeth 107:25; 148:8; Job 38:22,23; Jon 1:4; Joh 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-8","title":"Psalms 135:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>smote. 78:51; 105:36; 136:10; Ex 12:12,29,30; 13:15 both of man and beast. Heb. from man unto beast.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-9","title":"Psalms 135:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>sent tokens. 78:43-50; 105:27-29; Ex 7:1-15:27; De 4:34; Ne 9:10; Isa 51:9,10 Jer 32:20,21; Ac 7:36 upon Pharaoh. 136:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-10","title":"Psalms 135:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>smote. 44:2,3; 136:17-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-11","title":"Psalms 135:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Sihon. Nu 21:21-35; De 2:30-37; 3:1-11; Ne 9:22 and all the. Jos 10:1-12:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-12","title":"Psalms 135:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>gave their. 44:1-3; 78:55; 136:21,22; Nu 33:54; Jos 11:23; 12:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-13","title":"Psalms 135:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Thy name. 8:1,9; 72:17; 102:12,21; Ex 3:15; 34:5-7; Ho 12:5; Mt 6:9,13 throughout all generations. Heb. to generations andgenerations. 89:1; *marg:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-14","title":"Psalms 135:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>the Lord. 7:8; 50:4; 96:13 he will repent. De 32:36; Jud 10:16; 1Ch 21:15; Ho 11:8,9; Am 7:3,6; Jon 4:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-15","title":"Psalms 135:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>idols. 115:4-8; De 4:28; Isa 37:19; 40:19,20; 44:9-20; 46:6,7; Jer 10:3-11 Hab 2:18,19; Ac 17:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-16","title":"Psalms 135:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>eyes have they. Isa 6:10; Mt 13:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-18","title":"Psalms 135:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>They that. 97:7; 115:8; Isa 44:18-20; Jer 10:8; 2Co 4:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-19","title":"Psalms 135:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>115:9-11; 118:1-4; 145:10; 147:19,20; 148:14; Re 19:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-135-21","title":"Psalms 135:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":135,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":135,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>out of Zion. 76:2; 134:3; 2Ch 6:6 which dwelleth. 48:1,9; 132:13,14; Isa 12:6</p>"}]}